      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ENJABONARLO (8) was well in the betting when resuming in a Vicbred heat at Kilmore but little went his way and he faded out. He is much better than that having ended last campaign with a win from a similar barrier to this, taking his strike rate at this circuit and distance to 50 per cent. Can bounce back. PARTY CENTRAL NZ (6) is racing well and looks close to a win after seconds in his last two outings at this circuit and distance, coming from this barrier to miss narrowly last week. Big chance to atone. FASTING (7) is flying at present with two successive wins to his name. Draws wider than when he beat Party Central last week but with even luck he could keep the ball rolling. SAN SEBASTIAN (5) has claims off a dominant win at Newcastle last month.",
